  {
   "id": "a002",
   "anaphores": 4,
   "traduit": true,
   "traduction": "She then caught sight of a little glass box that was lying under the table, opened it, and found in it a very small cake"
  },
  {
   "id": "a003",
   "anaphores": 5,
   "traduit": true,
   "traduction": "So she ate a small piece of the cake, and, putting her hand on her head, she said to herself quite anxiously: \"Which one"
  },
  {
   "id": "a004",
   "anaphores": 2,
   "traduit": true,
   "traduction": "ALICE, sitting beside her sister on the grass, was beginning to get bored of staying there doing nothing."
  },
  {
   "id": "a005",
   "anaphores": 3,
   "traduit": true,
   "traduction": "Suddenly she met on her way a little three-legged table, all made of solid glass, and nothing on it but a tiny golden ke"
  },
  {
   "id": "a006",
   "anaphores": 3,
   "traduit": true,
   "traduction": "As it was no use spending her time waiting at the little door, she went back to the table, almost hoping to find another"
  },
  {
   "id": "a007",
   "anaphores": 2,
   "traduit": true,
   "traduction": "It's easy enough to say \"Drink me\", but Alice was too clever to obey blindly."
  },
  {
   "id": "a008",
   "anaphores": 5,
   "traduit": true,
   "traduction": "\"I feel all funny,\" said Alice, \"it looks as if I'm going back into myself and closing up like a telescope.\""
  },
  {
   "id": "a009",
   "anaphores": 7,
